// EXPECT-RUNTIME-ERROR: call depth exceeded
//
// S9 regression: the generated C used to write past the frame array on deep
// recursion, because every push was an unchecked `frame[sp] = ...; sp++`.
// ASan-confirmed stack-buffer-overflow (READ of size 24) at about 500 frames;
// the frame array is now a global that ASTRA_PUSH measures against.
//
// Since audit §1.1 (PRE_LLVM_AUDIT.md) the C backend also mirrors the VM's
// call-depth bound (ASTRA_CALL_DEPTH == VM_CALL_DEPTH), so this program stops
// with the VM's own "call depth exceeded" at the same call site. Before that
// guard the compiled side ran on until the operand stack gave out and worded
// the failure differently ("frame stack overflow"), which let the C backend
// happily run programs the VM rejected — countdown(300) printed 300.
//
// The runner checks that the generated program exits 1 with a "runtime error"
// line rather than a signal: a crash would exit non-zero too, so requiring the
// clean diagnostic is the whole point of the test. The operand-stack bound
// itself is pinned by stack_overflow_limit.astra (both directories).
fn countdown(n: i32) -> i32 {
    if n <= 0 { return 0 }
    return countdown(n - 1) + 1
}

fn main() {
    print(countdown(2000))
}
